           "t": "html",
           "items": [
            {
             "t": "h3",
             "html": "Context"
            },
            {
             "t": "p",
             "html": "This project was a part of a Design Challenge for the Innovation, Technology, &amp; Design program. We were tasked to identify a problem affecting a specific population at the University of Miami, design a solution, and create a business opportunity out of it. Deliverables included conducting user research, designing a prototype, creating a business plan, and pitching the product. This case study will focus on the UX Design and Research portion."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "t": "col",
         "span": 1,
         "kids": []
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "t": "hr"
  },
  {
   "t": "row",
   "cols": [
    {
     "t": "col",
     "span": 1,
     "kids": []
    },
    {
     "t": "col",
     "span": 11,
     "kids": [
      {
       "t": "row",
       "cols": [
        {
         "t": "col",
         "span": 10,
         "kids": [
          {
           "t": "html",
           "items": [
            {
             "t": "h3",
             "html": "Problem"
            },
            {
             "t": "h1",
             "html": "Change is wanted, but needs are <strong>NOT</strong> being voiced effectively"
            },
            {
             "t": "p",
             "html": "Currently, University of Miami requires all students who live on campus to have a meal plan. Students have a fixed number of meal swipes per week to use at 2 dining halls and are unhappy with the meal plans because they feel that the food isn’t enjoyable. However, <strong>they are not expressing their frustrations to the dining services in an effective way</strong>. The lack of specific feedback from students hampers the dining team’s ability to identify the core issues within the dining halls that contribute to student dissatisfaction. As a result, <strong>dining services struggle to understand the necessary changes required to enhance the overall dining experience</strong> for students."
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        },
        {
         "t": "col",
         "span": 1,
         "kids": []
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
